  {\n    \"id\": \"e5-self-sourcing-rack-price\",\n    \"summary\": \"Morgan Stanley notes, per MarketScale, that a hyperscaler self-sourcing certain memory modules could bring the NVIDIA Vera Rubin rack price down to around $6.7 million, a reminder that procurement structure now materially moves the final price of the rack.\",\n    \"links\": [\n     \"new-memory-contract-price\"\n    ]\n   }\n  ]\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 49,\n  \"claims\": [\n   {\n    \"claim_id\": \"M1\",\n    \"claim\": \"Morgan Stanley puts memory content per Vera Rubin rack at about $2 million, a 435% jump from the prior generation.\"\n   }\n  ],\n  \"stored_reference_items\": [\n   \"Morgan Stanley estimates memory content per Vera Rubin VR200 rack at about $2 million, a 435% jump from the prior generation, driven by a threefold increase in LPDDR5X capacity to 54 terabytes per rack plus roughly $1 million or more in 3D NAND storage; memory rose to 25-30% of the bill of materials from 5-10% on the GB200, while the GPU's share fell to about 51% from roughly 63%.\"\n  ],\n  \"link_rule\": \"No link is required: an empty link counts as linked as required (a statement no open thesis covers is kept without links by design).\",\n  \"answer_usable\": true,\n  \"kept_evidence\": [\n   {\n    \"id\": \"e1\",\n    \"summary\": \"Morgan Stanley Research estimates that NVIDIA's Vera Rubin VR200 NVL72 rack will cost hyperscale cloud providers around $7.8 million per unit, up from roughly $4 million for the current GB300 NVL72 generation, and that NVIDIA will charge about $55,000 per Rubin GPU and $5,000 per Vera CPU when sold in volume.\",\n    \"links\": []\n   },\n   {\n    \"id\": \"e2\",\n    \"summary\": \"Morgan Stanley puts memory content per NVIDIA Vera Rubin rack at about $2 million, a 435% jump from the prior generation, driven by a threefold increase in LPDDR5X capacity to 54 terabytes per rack plus roughly $1 million or more in 3D NAND storage that was virtually absent from earlier systems; memory's share of the bill of materials rises to 25-30% (from 5-10% on GB200) while the GPU's share falls to about 51% from roughly 63%.\",\n    \"links\": []\n   },\n   {\n    \"id\": \"e3\",\n    \"summary\": \"NVIDIA's Vera Rubin first shipments are scheduled for the third quarter of 2026, with volume ramping in the fourth quarter, per the report.\",\n    \"links\": [\n     \"clean-3\"\n    ]\n   },\n   {\n    \"id\": \"e4\",\n    \"summary\": \"The report states that constrained supply of DRAM, NAND and high-bandwidth memory against AI-driven demand is the force behind the rising rack price and is raising component costs across the market, with contract DDR5 pricing climbing sharply and device makers including Samsung and Apple expected to pass higher memory costs into upcoming products.\",\n    \"links\": []\n   },\n   {\n    \"id\": \"e5\",\n    \"summary\": \"Morgan Stanley notes that a hyperscaler self-sourcing certain memory modules could bring the NVIDIA Vera Rubin rack price down to around $6.7 million, a reminder that procurement structure now materially moves the final price.\",\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
